### FINDING-2: [clampInt](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminScout.ts#541-546) Duplication with Inconsistent Signatures (8 Copies)

**Severity: HIGH** — The same utility function is copy-pasted 8 times with **different argument orders**, creating a latent bug risk.

| File | Signature |
|------|-----------|
| [shared/scalars.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/shared/scalars.ts) | [clampInt(raw, fallback, min, max)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminScout.ts#541-546) ✅ canonical |
| [server/services/adminAuditTrail.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/services/adminAuditTrail.ts) | [clampInt(raw, fallback, min, max)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminScout.ts#541-546) |
| [server/services/rememberMe.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/services/rememberMe.ts) | [clampInt(value, fallback, min, max)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminScout.ts#541-546) |
| [server/services/globalSettingsAdmin.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/services/globalSettingsAdmin.ts) | [clampInt(value, min, max, fallback)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminScout.ts#541-546) ⚠️ **different order** |
| [server/routes/adminInstitutionalAudit.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminInstitutionalAudit.ts) | [clampInt(raw, fallback, min, max)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminScout.ts#541-546) |
| [server/routes/adminScout/support.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminScout/support.ts) | [clampInt(value, fallback, min, max)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminScout.ts#541-546) |
| [server/routes/adminActivity.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminActivity.ts) | [clampInt(v, lo, hi, fallback)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminScout.ts#541-546) ⚠️ **different order** |
| [server/cron/evaluateChallenges.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/cron/evaluateChallenges.ts) | [clampInt(value, fallback, min, max)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminScout.ts#541-546) |
| [server/grift/griftRetention.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/grift/griftRetention.ts) | [clampInt(value, min, max, fallback)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminScout.ts#541-546) ⚠️ **different order** |

**3 out of 8 copies** have [(value, min, max, fallback)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/services/adminDataExportBuild.ts#348-353) while the canonical version uses [(raw, fallback, min, max)](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/services/adminDataExportBuild.ts#348-353). Any call site swapping between implementations would silently produce wrong clamping behavior.

