## 3. Architecture Quality Assessment

### ✅ What's Well-Done

| Area | Assessment |
|------|-----------|
| **Trade lifecycle safety** | Transaction-locked with `SELECT FOR UPDATE`, quote revalidation at commit, stale-quote rejection |
| **Audit trail completeness** | Hash-chained SHA-256, ORDER_RECEIVED → DECISION → ORDER_FILLED/REJECTED events |
| **Auth/session security** | Token theft detection, rotation, idle timeout, IP rate limiting, impersonation write-blocking |
| **CSRF protection** | Proper double-submit cookie with triple-check (cookie + header + session) |
| **Policy enforcement** | Single `decidePolicy()` source of truth, middleware-based with full deny audit trail |
| **Margin/risk system** | Floating PnL incorporated, stale-close defaults to deny, configurable thresholds |
| **Cost model** | Full open/close settlement costs with financing, swap, overnight accrual |
| **Excursion tracking** | Migrated to Valkey/Redis for horizontal scalability |
| **Clean code hygiene** | 0 TODO/FIXME/HACK comments found in entire codebase |

### ⚠️ Concerns

| Area | Issue |
|------|-------|
| **TypeScript safety** | 42 files bypass compiler, 69 `as any` in core trade paths |
| **Code duplication** | [clampInt](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/adminScout.ts#541-546) 8x with inconsistent signatures; pattern likely exists for others |
| **File size** | 37 files exceed 1,000 LOC; 13 exceed 2,000 LOC |
| **Test coverage** | Critical business logic (trade lifecycle, risk, policy, grift) has 0 unit tests |
| **[traderCore.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/traderCore.ts)** | 1,719-line single function — impossible to unit test, review, or safely modify |

